==Description== <!--T:2-->

<!--T:6-->
The [[Image:Sketcher_EditSketch.svg|24px]] [[Sketcher_EditSketch|Sketcher EditSketch]] tool opens the [[Sketcher_Dialog|Sketcher Dialog]] to edit an existing sketch.

==Usage== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:7-->
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Double-click a sketch in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]].
#* Select a sketch and press the {{Button|[[Image:Sketcher_EditSketch.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_EditSketch|Edit Sketch]]}} button.
#* Select a sketch and then select the {{MenuCommand|Sketch → [[Image:Sketcher_EditSketch.svg|16px]] Edit Sketch}} option from the menu.
#* Right-click a sketch in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] and select the {{MenuCommand|Edit Sketch}} option from the context menu.
# The sketch is put in edit mode and the [[Sketcher_Dialog|Sketcher Dialog]] opens.
# To finish edit mode see [[Image:Sketcher_LeaveSketch.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_LeaveSketch|Sketcher LeaveSketch]].

{{Version|26.3}}: To restore the view while a sketch is already in edit mode, double-click that sketch in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]]. This runs [[Sketcher_ViewSketch|Align View to Sketch]] without ending the edit session.

==Editing sketches in different documents==

{{Version|26.3}}: Sketches in different documents can remain in edit mode at the same time. To work on two sketches:

# Open both documents and put a sketch in the first document in edit mode.
# Select the second document's tab in the main view area, then put a sketch in that document in edit mode.
# Switch between the document tabs to continue editing either sketch. The [[Sketcher_Dialog|Sketcher Dialog]] changes to match the active document, and switching away from a document does not finish its sketch edit session.

To finish editing one sketch, activate its document and use [[Sketcher_LeaveSketch|Leave Sketch]] or the dialog's {{Button|Close}} button. Sketches being edited in other documents remain in edit mode.


